    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0872" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/10–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-26T13:00:00+01:00">October 26, 1948—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 26—8:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Martel</hi> 86. Instructions to Stuart in <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Telmar</hi> 100<anchor n="15" xml:id="d764-f1"/>
                    approved. As to <hi rendition="#small-caps">Telmar</hi> 98,<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d764-f2"/> Dr. Wang<anchor n="17" xml:id="d764-f3"/> appealed to me
                    yesterday along lines of <pb facs="0873" n="863" xml:id="pg863"/>
                    Generalissimo’s appeal reference American dependents. The issue here involves
                    two factors, one the destructive effect on public of such an announcement and
                    second, responsibilities for safety of American women and children. For this
                    reason I do not entirely agree with placing of complete responsibility on Stuart
                    as indicated in second sentence of <hi rendition="#small-caps">Telmar</hi>
                        98.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d764-f4"/> We must share responsibility of
                    decision. Stuart must judge degree of danger and we must judge demoralizing
                    effect of such announcement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d764-f1" n="15" xml:id="d764-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for text of instructions, see telegram No. 1488, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f2" n="16" xml:id="d764-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 1, <ref target="#pg859">p. 859</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f3" n="17" xml:id="d764-f3-content">
                <p>Wang Shih-chieh, Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs, then in Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d764-f4" n="18" xml:id="d764-f4-content">
                <p>Apparently reference to second sentence of telegram No. 1485, October 24, 8 p.m.,
                    to the Ambassador in China, <ref target="#pg860">p. 860</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
